{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "cluster_aware_hybrid",
  "intent": "Add cluster_density as a tertiary bias to the parent's return_aware + regret blend. High cluster_density (fraction of unvisited cities within mean distance) signals dense neighborhoods worth compacting into local subtours rather than wandering across voids. The 0.1 magnitude keeps it below the -d primary anchor and the r/g secondary signals, preserving greedy primacy. Targeting the family's weakest axis (clustered at 0.052) without inflating uniform/grid noise; cluster_density is near-uniform on uniform instances, so it acts mainly when structure exists.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "return_aware"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    r = f['return_distance']\n    g = f['regret']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + 0.25 * r + 0.15 * g + 0.1 * cd",
